        "id": 1108919
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-18T03:59:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we\u0027ve had a few of the fuzzers fail for over-allocating on the stack.\nlet\u0027s allocate this in the heap instead.\n\nalso thinking out loud about size bytes of input to size bytes of output -- and whether\nwe believe that the encoded data will always be smaller than the input. i can imagine that for certain very small inputs, the output will include some preamble + the encoded bits.\nand while \"encoded bits\" might always be smaller than \u0027input\u0027, not sure about whatever preamble....\n\nso let\u0027s think about whether the output buffer needs to be larger.\non the other hand -- if it\u0027s too small in some configurations, that does test whether\nthe codec is stopping in time....",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 160,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 160,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "13d11e8e58507764b3cbbad840b10147af2e470d",
